        "original_id": "0a40c1b0-3ee5-511c-bb88-762a684073cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Bowie, Tony Visconti\n- Products: Blackstar, Dollar Days\n- Places: New York City, The Magic Shop, Human Worldwide Studios\n- Topics: Death of David Bowie, album recording, liver cancer\n\nFacts:\n- Blackstar was released on 8 January 2016 as David Bowie's twenty-fifth studio album, and its release coincided with his 69th birthday.\n- Dollar Days is the sixth track on David Bowie's twenty-fifth and final studio album, Blackstar.\n- Blackstar was largely recorded in secret in New York City at The Magic Shop and Human Worldwide Studios with David Bowie's longtime co-producer Tony Visconti and a group of local jazz musicians.\n- On 10 January 2016, David Bowie died at his apartment in New York City after suffering from liver cancer for the previous 18 months.\n- David Bowie's death occurred two days after the release of Blackstar.",
